# Services

Adafruit IO provides a few integrated services that you can use with your AIO key: [Weather](#weather), [Air Quality](#air-quality), [Randomizer](#randomizer), [Messages (SMS)](#messages-sms), [Time](#time), and an [Image Formatter](#image-formatter).

Weather, Air Quality, Randomizer and Messages work by creating an *integration record*. Once a record exists, Adafruit IO publishes its data to MQTT topics, and you can also read it over HTTP with the endpoints below. These endpoints are for scripts and devices using an AIO key, and requests from other websites (cross-origin browser requests) are rejected.

IFTTT is set up from the [IFTTT](https://io.adafruit.com/services/ifttt) service page and the Adafruit IO service on ifttt.com, not through this API. There is no Zapier integration.

## Time

The Adafruit IO time service does not replace a time-synchronization service like NTP, but it can help you figure out your local time on an Internet of Things device that doesn't have a built in clock. Time is also published on [MQTT time topics](mqtt.html#time-topics).

### Unauthenticated Time

These endpoints don't need an AIO key and return plain text (not JSON), always in UTC.

#### Get Time in Seconds

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/time/seconds</code></div>

```shell
$ curl https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/time/seconds
```

> Response Sample:

```text
1760368123
```

Current Unix time in whole seconds.

#### Get Time in Milliseconds

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/time/millis</code></div>

```shell
$ curl https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/time/millis
```

> Response Sample:

```text
1760368123456
```

Current Unix time in milliseconds.

#### Get Time in ISO-8601

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/time/ISO-8601</code></div>

```shell
$ curl https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/time/ISO-8601
```

> Response Sample:

```text
2026-10-13T14:28:43Z
```

Current UTC time as an ISO-8601 string.

#### Get Time (JSON or Text)

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/utilities/time</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "Accept: application/json" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/utilities/time
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "iso8601": "2026-10-13T14:28:43Z",
  "rfc822": "Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:28:43 +0000",
  "millis": 1760368123
}
```

Returns the current UTC time in three formats. Request JSON with `Accept: application/json` (or a `.json` extension). Request text with `Accept: text/plain` (or a `.txt` extension), which returns a single value chosen by the `output` query parameter: `iso8601`, `rfc822`, or, if `output` is omitted, the `millis` value. Note that the `millis` value is Unix time in **seconds**, not milliseconds. Use `/api/v2/time/millis` for milliseconds.

### Query Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
output | string | false | Text responses only: `iso8601` or `rfc822`. Defaults to the `millis` value.

### Time in Your Time Zone

These endpoints need your AIO key. They return the current time in a time zone, which is picked in this order: the `tz` parameter, then a lookup from your request's IP address, then UTC.

#### List Time Zones and Links

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time?tz=America/New_York
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "zones": ["Africa/Abidjan", "Africa/Accra", "..."],
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "time": "2026-10-13T10:28:43-04:00",
  "links": {
    "strftime": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/strftime",
    "clock": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/clock",
    "struct": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/struct"
  }
}
```

Lists every valid time zone name, the time zone in use, and the current time there.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Query Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
tz | string | false | A time zone name such as `America/New_York`. An invalid name returns a `400` that lists every valid name.

#### Get Time as ISO-8601 (Clock)

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/clock</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/clock?tz=America/New_York
```

> Response Sample:

```text
2026-10-13T10:28:43-04:00
```

Plain text ISO-8601 time with the zone offset. Accepts `tz`.

#### Get Time as a Struct

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/struct</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/struct?tz=America/New_York
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{"year":2026,"mon":10,"mday":13,"hour":10,"min":28,"sec":43,"wday":2,"yday":286,"isdst":1}
```

Broken-down time. `wday` is 0 for Sunday through 6 for Saturday, `yday` starts at 1, and `isdst` is 1 during daylight saving time and 0 otherwise. Accepts `tz`.

#### Get Formatted Time (strftime)

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/strftime</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/time/strftime?tz=America/New_York&string=%25Y-%25m-%25d%20%25H:%25M"
```

> Response Sample:

```text
2026-10-13 10:28
```

Plain text time formatted with a [strftime](https://ruby-doc.org/core/Time.html#method-i-strftime) format string. A missing, invalid or too long format returns a `422`.

### Query Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
string | string | true | The format string, at most 64 characters. Remember to URL-encode `%`.
tz | string | false | A time zone name such as `America/New_York`.

## Randomizer

Randomizer records generate random words, numbers, colors, or a pick from a list of values you choose. Each record is also published on the [randomizer MQTT topic](mqtt.html#randomizer-topics). The randomizer is available on Free and IO+ accounts, with up to 20 enabled records per user.

Values change in 30 second time slices: the same record returns the same value within a slice, and two records with the same settings and `seed` produce the same values. Each `GET` of a single record generates a value.

### List Randomizer Records

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 42,
    "value_type": "number",
    "value": 5731,
    "seed": "Jx3Rk9pQzLw2mT7a",
    "time_slice": 1760368110,
    "links": {
      "mqtt": "{username}/integration/words/42",
      "self": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/42"
    },
    "value_minimum": 1000,
    "value_maximum": 9999
  }
]
```

Lists your enabled randomizer records, each with a newly generated `value`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Create a Randomizer Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"word": {"value_type": "number", "value_minimum": 1000, "value_maximum": 9999}}' https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 42,
  "value_type": "number",
  "value": 5731,
  "seed": "Jx3Rk9pQzLw2mT7a",
  "time_slice": 1760368110,
  "links": {
    "mqtt": "{username}/integration/words/42",
    "self": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/42"
  },
  "value_minimum": 1000,
  "value_maximum": 9999
}
```

Creates a record. Send the parameters below inside a `word` object. Invalid input returns a `422` with the errors.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Body Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
value_type | string | true | `word`, `number`, `color`, or `preset`.
seed | string | false | Seed for the generator. A random one is created if omitted.
value_minimum | integer | false | `number`: lowest value. `word`: minimum word length. Zero or greater.
value_maximum | integer | false | `number`: highest value. `word`: maximum word length (default 16). Zero or greater. With no minimum or maximum, `number` returns a decimal between 0 and 1.
value_mode | integer | color only | Color format: `0` RGB, `1` HSL, `2` CSS hex, `3` CSS color name.
collection | array or string | preset only | The values to choose from, as an array or a comma-separated string.

### Get a Randomizer Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/42
```

Returns one record in the same format as Create, with a newly generated `value`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the randomizer record.

### Delete a Randomizer Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X DELETE -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/words/42
```

Permanently deletes the record and returns it.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the randomizer record.

## Weather

Weather data comes from Apple WeatherKit. **Requires IO+**, with up to 5 enabled weather records per account. Data for a record is cached and refreshed at most once every 20 minutes. The same data is published to the [weather MQTT topics](mqtt.html#weather-topics-io), so reading it over HTTP is optional.

A record is identified by a numeric `id`. Its `links.mqtt` field lists the MQTT topic for each forecast: `current`, `forecast_minutes_5`, `forecast_minutes_30`, `forecast_hours_1`, `forecast_hours_2`, `forecast_hours_6`, `forecast_hours_12`, `forecast_hours_24`, `forecast_days_1`, `forecast_days_2`, and `forecast_days_5`.

### List Weather Records

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 7,
    "location": "40.7128,-74.006",
    "name": "Home",
    "last_request_at": "2026-10-13T14:10:02.000Z",
    "last_request_status": "200",
    "links": {
      "mqtt": {
        "current": "{username}/integration/weather/7/current",
        "forecast_hours_1": "{username}/integration/weather/7/forecast_hours_1"
      },
      "self": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/7"
    }
  }
]
```

Lists your enabled weather records without forecast values (the `mqtt` map is shortened here). **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Create a Weather Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"weather": {"location": "40.7128,-74.0060", "name": "Home"}}' https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather
```

Returns the new record in the format shown above. Send the parameters below inside a `weather` object. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`. A bad location, a duplicate `name`, or going over the 5 record limit returns a `422`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Body Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
location | string | true | `latitude,longitude` in decimal degrees.
name | string | false | A friendly name, unique among your weather records.

### Get a Weather Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/7
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "location": "40.7128,-74.006",
  "name": "Home",
  "last_request_at": "2026-10-13T14:10:02.000Z",
  "last_request_status": "200",
  "current": {"temperature": 18.4, "conditionCode": "PartlyCloudy", "humidity": 0.62, "...": "..."},
  "forecast_hours_1": {"temperature": 17.9, "...": "..."},
  "links": {"mqtt": {"current": "{username}/integration/weather/7/current"}, "self": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/7"}
}
```

Returns the record with the current conditions and each forecast (shortened above). The forecast objects are WeatherKit data and are `null` when no data is available. Responses can be up to 20 minutes old. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the weather record.

### Delete a Weather Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X DELETE -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/weather/7
```

Permanently deletes the record and returns it. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the weather record.

## Air Quality

Get real-time air quality measurements and forecasts. **Requires IO+**, with up to 5 enabled air quality records per account. Data for a record is cached and refreshed at most once every 20 minutes. The same data is published to the [air quality MQTT topics](mqtt.html#air-quality-topics-io): `current`, `forecast_today` and `forecast_tomorrow`.

### List Air Quality Records

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 3,
    "location": "40.7128,-74.006",
    "name": "Home",
    "last_request_at": "2026-10-13T14:10:02.000Z",
    "last_request_status": "200",
    "provider": "open_meteo",
    "links": {
      "mqtt": {
        "current": "{username}/integration/air_quality/3/current",
        "forecast_today": "{username}/integration/air_quality/3/forecast_today",
        "forecast_tomorrow": "{username}/integration/air_quality/3/forecast_tomorrow"
      },
      "self": "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality/3"
    }
  }
]
```

Lists your enabled air quality records without their current forecast values. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Create an Air Quality Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"air_quality": {"location": "40.7128,-74.0060", "name": "Home", "provider": "open_meteo"}}' https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality
```

Returns the new record in the format shown above. Send the parameters below inside an `air_quality` object. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`. A bad location, duplicate `name`, invalid `provider`, or going over the 5 record limit returns a `422`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Body Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
location | string | true | `latitude,longitude` in decimal degrees.
name | string | false | A friendly name, unique among your air quality records.
provider | string | false | `open_meteo` (global coverage, the default) or `airnow` (US only, official EPA data).

### Get an Air Quality Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality/3
```

Returns the record with `current`, `forecast_today` and `forecast_tomorrow` air quality values, including pollutants such as PM2.5, PM10, ozone and nitrogen dioxide. The values are `null` when no data is available. Responses can be up to 20 minutes old. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the air quality record.

### Delete an Air Quality Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/air_quality/{id}</code></div>

