## Messages (SMS)

Lets you save data to a feed by texting Adafruit IO. Text a message in the form `feed-key, value` to the Adafruit IO number from your verified phone number. The value is saved to that feed, and you get a text back with an acknowledgement. Texting just a feed key replies with the feed's last value. **Requires IO+**, and each account can have 1 SMS record. Texts are limited to 25 per day per account, and texts over the limit are not saved. Errors are reported to your monitor page.

The phone number must be verified in your account settings first. The record always uses your verified phone number, and the number in responses is masked.

### List Message Records

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "service_name": "sms",
    "service_endpoint": "•••••••7777",
    "last_message_at": "2026-10-13T14:00:00.000Z",
    "last_message_status": "OK"
  }
]
```

Lists your enabled message records. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Create a Message Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"message": {"service_name": "sms"}}' https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages
```

Creates an SMS record for your verified phone number and returns it. Returns a `422` if you have no verified phone number or are over the record limit. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.

### Body Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
service_name | string | true | Must be `sms`, sent inside a `message` object.

### Get a Message Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages/1
```

Returns one message record. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the message record.

### Delete a Message Record

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X DELETE -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/messages/1
```

Permanently deletes the record and returns it. **Requires IO+.** Free accounts get a `403`.

### Path Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
username | string | true | Your Adafruit IO username. Must match the owner of the key.
id | integer | true | The id of the message record.

## Image Formatter

Downloads an image from a public URL, resizes it, and returns it as a BMP file, which is handy for small displays on microcontrollers. Available on Free and IO+ accounts.

Limits: the source image can be at most 1 MB and must be at a public `http://` or `https://` URL (private and internal addresses are rejected). Free accounts can make 1 request per 60 seconds, and IO+ accounts 1 request per 5 seconds. Extra requests get a `429`.

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/integrations/image-formatter</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -o image.bmp "https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/integrations/image-formatter?url=https://example.com/photo.jpg&width=128&height=64&output=BMP16"
```

Returns the image (`Content-Type: image/bmp`). A `POST` with the same parameters also works. A bad parameter, an image that can't be loaded or is too large returns a `422` with a message.

### Query Parameters

Parameter | Type | Required | Description
--------- | ---- | -------- | -----------
url | string | true | Public URL of the source image.
width | integer | true | Output width in pixels. Positive integer.
height | integer | true | Output height in pixels. Positive integer.
output | string | true | Bit depth: `BMP1`, `BMP8`, `BMP16`, `BMP24` or `BMP32`.
